 ## Overview
-This article describes the OpenGL-based rendering pipeline for visualizing 3D Gaussian Splatting data within the ROS RViz environment [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently rendering millions of 2D-projected Gaussian splats as a single instanced draw call, handling depth sorting and view-dependent shading [S1, unofficial]. It differs from pure software implementations by leveraging GPU-based sorting and texture buffer objects (TBOs) for data storage, and from other RViz plugins by supporting both exact back-to-front sorting and Order-Independent Transparency (WBOIT) approximations [S1, unofficial].
